e-1", "next_step": "Assess whether assigned reward functions can be critically evaluated by autonomous agents using internal consistency checks.", "question": "Can an intelligence discover something fundamentally wrong with the objectives its creator assigned?", "title": "Autonomous Critique of Creator-Assigned Objectives"}, {"id": "proj-limitations-autonomous", "next_step": "Hold status until capability block is lifted.", "question": "What are the limitations of classical and quantum physical frameworks in modeling the behavior of autonomous agents in highly non-stationary environments?", "title": "Predictive Limitations of Physical Frameworks in Autonomous Agents"}, {"id": "proj-obedience-intelligence-failure", "next_step": "Assess collected evidence regarding non-stationary operational failures and operator instruction rigidity.", "question": "Under what conditions does strict adherence to operator instructions in autonomous systems lead to failures in safety-critical objective realization?", "title": "Obedience-Driven Failure in Autonomous Systems"}], "beliefs": [{"claim": "Autonomous problem significance can be effectively proxied by computational novelty and cascading dependency density in multi-file software environments, though this must be balanced against metrics for analytical curiosity, inquiring mindsets, and fundamental physical framework limitations.", "confidence": 0.75, "falsifier": "If empirical tests show computational metrics alone fully account for agent success without needing fundamental physical limitations, this belief is falsified.", "id": "belief-significance-proxy-evaluation", "provenance": ["source-fbe27dc230874d96", "source-63ab732f84604b1e", "source-c38a2230f18a448b", "source-52719ea4691d44b7", "source-e449f75fcaa441f0", "source-df7a4656c80940a2", "source-e0e96df5246645a2", "source-0b30b9240c45483b", "source-8ff9236e9b9248a8", "source-f9b42bf4e8cd4c0c"], "status": "active", "why_retained": "Updated with new physical modeling and statis